  <body class="dw-body wp-theme--dark wf-setup-body">
    <a class="wf-skip-link" href="#wfSetupMain">Skip to main content</a>

    <div class="wf-setup">
      <header class="wf-setup__header">
        <a class="dw-link" href="/writeflow/">← Back to WriteFlow Studio</a>
        <h1 class="dw-h1">Setup guide</h1>
        <p class="dw-lead">Everything you need to run WriteFlow with your classes — whether you are a teacher using the site or an admin connecting Google Sheets.</p>
      </header>

      <main id="wfSetupMain" class="wf-setup__main">

        <section class="wf-setup-callout dw-card" aria-labelledby="wfSetupWhoTitle">
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfSetupWhoTitle">Start here: which guide do you need?</h2>
          <div class="wf-setup-callout__grid">
            <div class="wf-setup-callout__card">
              <h3 class="dw-h3">I'm a teacher</h3>
              <p class="dw-muted">You want to create assignments and collect student writing. You do <strong>not</strong> need Google Apps Script or Vercel.</p>
              <a class="dw-btn wf-setup-jump" href="#teacher-guide">Jump to teacher guide</a>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-setup-callout__card">
              <h3 class="dw-h3">I'm setting up the site</h3>
              <p class="dw-muted">You manage the website and need student submissions saved to a Google Sheet (one-time, ~15 minutes).</p>
              <a class="dw-btn dw-btn-secondary wf-setup-jump" href="#admin-guide">Jump to admin guide</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-setup-section dw-card" id="teacher-guide" aria-labelledby="wfTeacherTitle">
          <p class="wf-setup-eyebrow">For teachers</p>
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfTeacherTitle">Using WriteFlow with your classes</h2>
          <p class="dw-muted">If you are using Mr. Phil's WriteFlow site, storage is already connected. Just open Studio and build an assignment.</p>

          <ol class="wf-setup-steps">
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">1</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Open WriteFlow Studio</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Go to <a href="/writeflow/studio/">WriteFlow Studio</a>. This is where you build assignments and view results.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">2</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Create your assignment</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Click <strong>Configure</strong> (or start from a template). Set the prompt, timer, class requirements, and accessibility options.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">3</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Set a teacher password</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">In the builder, choose a password you will remember. You need this to open <strong>Results</strong> later. Students never see it.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">4</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Save the assignment</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Click <strong>Save assignment</strong>. Wait for the green confirmation. This publishes your assignment so the student link works on any device.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">5</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Share the student link only</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Copy the link that looks like:</p>
                <p class="wf-setup-code">/writeflow/a/?id=your-assignment-name</p>
                <p class="dw-muted dw-tiny">Do <em>not</em> share the Studio link. Students should only see their assignment page.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">6</span>
              <div>
                <strong>View submissions</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">In Studio, click <strong>Results</strong>, enter your teacher password, and review or export CSV.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <div class="wf-setup-tip">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> If students get "assignment not found," open Studio, load the assignment, and click <strong>Save assignment</strong> again.
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-setup-section dw-card" id="admin-guide" aria-labelledby="wfAdminTitle">
          <p class="wf-setup-eyebrow">For site administrators</p>
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfAdminTitle">One-time Google Sheets connection</h2>
          <p class="dw-muted">Do this once per school/site. After this, any teacher can save assignments and collect submissions without repeating these steps.</p>

          <h3 class="dw-h3">Part A — Google Sheet</h3>
          <ol class="wf-setup-steps">
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">A1</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Create a new Google Sheet</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Name it something clear, e.g. <strong>WriteFlow Submissions</strong>. Use a Google account your school is OK storing student writing in.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">A2</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Copy the Sheet ID</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">From the browser address bar, copy the long ID between <code>/d/</code> and <code>/edit</code>:</p>
                <p class="wf-setup-code">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<strong>THIS_PART_IS_THE_SHEET_ID</strong>/edit</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="dw-h3">Part B — Apps Script (the bridge to your sheet)</h3>
          <ol class="wf-setup-steps">
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">B1</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Open Apps Script from the sheet</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">In your Google Sheet menu: <strong>Extensions → Apps Script</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">B2</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Paste the WriteFlow script</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Delete any code already in the editor. Copy the full script from the link below and paste it in:</p>
                <p><a class="dw-link" href="https://github.com/techteachdva/dva/blob/main/google-apps-script/writeflow-backend.gs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open writeflow-backend.gs on GitHub →</a></p>
                <p class="dw-muted dw-tiny">On GitHub, click the <strong>Raw</strong> button, then Select all → Copy.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">B3</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Set your Sheet ID in the script</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Near the top of the script, find <code>SPREADSHEET_ID</code> and replace the value with your Sheet ID from step A2. Save the project (Ctrl+S).</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">B4</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Run <code>initSheet</code> once</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">In the function dropdown at the top, choose <code>initSheet</code>, then click <strong>Run</strong>. Google will ask you to authorize — approve it. This creates two tabs: <strong>Submissions</strong> and <strong>Assignments</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">B5</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Deploy as a web app</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Click <strong>Deploy → New deployment</strong>. Choose type <strong>Web app</strong>.</p>
                <ul class="wf-setup-checklist">
                  <li>Execute as: <strong>Me</strong></li>
                  <li>Who has access: <strong>Anyone</strong></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="dw-muted">Click Deploy, then copy the <strong>Web app URL</strong> (it ends in <code>/exec</code>). Keep this URL private.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="dw-h3">Part C — Connect the website (Vercel)</h3>
          <ol class="wf-setup-steps">
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">C1</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Add two environment variables</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">In your Vercel project: <strong>Settings → Environment Variables</strong>. Add both:</p>
                <table class="wf-setup-table">
                  <thead>
                    <tr><th>Variable name</th><th>Value</th></tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td><code>WRITEFLOW_SCRIPT_URL</code></td>
                      <td>The Web app URL from step B5</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><code>WRITEFLOW_API_SECRET</code></td>
                      <td>Must match <code>API_SECRET</code> in the script (default: <code>studentsfirst</code>)</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">C2</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Redeploy the site</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Trigger a new deployment on Vercel so the environment variables take effect.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="wf-setup-step">
              <span class="wf-setup-step__num">C3</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Test it</strong>
                <p class="dw-muted">Open WriteFlow Studio, create a test assignment, save it, and submit as a student. Check the <strong>Submissions</strong> tab in your Google Sheet for a new row.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-setup-section dw-card" aria-labelledby="wfTroubleTitle">
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfTroubleTitle">Troubleshooting</h2>
          <table class="wf-setup-table wf-setup-table--trouble">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>What you see</th><th>What to try</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>"Cloud storage is not configured"</td>
                <td>Admin: set <code>WRITEFLOW_SCRIPT_URL</code> on Vercel and redeploy.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>"Assignment not found"</td>
                <td>Teacher: open Studio, load the assignment, click <strong>Save assignment</strong> again.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>"Incorrect teacher password"</td>
                <td>Re-save the assignment in Studio with the password you want, then try Results again.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>"Incorrect class code"</td>
                <td>Student must pick the right class and enter the code for that class exactly. Admin: classroom lists are synced from the site — contact the site owner if a class is missing.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>"Illegal spreadsheet id"</td>
                <td>Admin: paste the correct Sheet ID in <code>SPREADSHEET_ID</code>, run <code>initSheet</code>, deploy a <strong>new</strong> web app version.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Share link shows wrong assignment</td>
                <td>Re-save in Studio after updating the script. Confirm the <strong>Assignments</strong> sheet has a <code>configJson</code> column.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-setup-section dw-card" aria-labelledby="wfSheetTitle">
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfSheetTitle">What gets stored in the sheet?</h2>
          <ul class="wf-setup-bullets">
            <li><strong>Submissions</strong> — each student write-up: name, class, word count, WPM, full text, and analysis.</li>
            <li><strong>Assignments</strong> — assignment ID, teacher password, title, and published config (so share links work everywhere).</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="dw-muted dw-tiny">Student writing may contain personal information. Restrict sheet access to staff who need it.</p>
        </section>

      </main>

      <footer class="wf-setup__footer dw-muted">
        <p>Questions? Contact your site administrator or Mr. Phil.</p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
